1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,730
In Unit, open Deployments and use Open to
review active assignments.

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:09,250
This example opens TRAINING ONLY, Academy
field operations.

3
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:13,609
Read the deployment name and reference
before continuing, especially when

4
00:00:13,609 --> 00:00:15,250
several crews share a vehicle.

5
00:00:15,659 --> 00:00:19,860
A fire or EMS crew can use this workspace
to organize a deployment;

6
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:23,920
the information shown here belongs to a
fictional software exercise.

7
00:00:24,109 --> 00:00:28,110
Inside the deployment, the Time tab shows
the Date, the selected

8
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:30,299
crew, and Reports this day.

9
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:34,989
Here, the displayed date is October
twenty-sixth and the Engine Fifty-One

10
00:00:34,989 --> 00:00:36,899
crew already has a Draft report.

11
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:40,029
Read that existing report before starting
another one.

12
00:00:40,389 --> 00:00:43,459
Its deployment roster is separate from the
apparatus staffing

13
00:00:43,459 --> 00:00:45,399
seats used for incident response.

14
00:00:45,519 --> 00:00:48,660
Scroll through the existing entries and
compare the From and

15
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:53,300
To values, Unpaid break, and agency
supplied meals and accommodation.

16
00:00:53,759 --> 00:00:57,799
The summary shows eight hours for the unit
and eight for Boden, totaling

17
00:00:57,799 --> 00:00:59,790
sixteen hours across subjects.

18
00:01:00,169 --> 00:01:02,130
These are existing training values.

19
00:01:02,579 --> 00:01:07,099
Apply to crew and Add entry are separate
editing choices; we leave the time

20
00:01:07,099 --> 00:01:08,979
entries and allowances as they are.

21
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:13,690
In the Engine Fifty-One row, use the note
field beneath the allowance switches.

22
00:01:14,049 --> 00:01:17,460
The example note identifies this as a
training walkthrough and

23
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:21,790
says it makes no actual hours, work,
expense, or payment claim.

24
00:01:22,269 --> 00:01:26,130
Check the subject name before typing: a
unit note and a personnel

25
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:28,009
note belong to different entries.

26
00:01:28,349 --> 00:01:32,460
This edit changes the unit note while
preserving the other displayed values.

27
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:36,409
Scroll below the entries and choose Save
entries to store the note.

28
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:41,049
Submit report is a different action, and
the Signatures section still says

29
00:01:41,049 --> 00:01:45,129
that the crew boss has not signed and no
agency signature is recorded.

30
00:01:45,539 --> 00:01:48,920
Saving an explanatory draft note does not
submit the report

31
00:01:48,959 --> 00:01:50,560
or provide an attestation.

32
00:01:50,949 --> 00:01:54,219
Keep those later actions separate when
reviewing a practice draft.

33
00:01:54,379 --> 00:01:58,519
After saving, this draft shows a
long-shift warning for each subject

34
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:00,229
because no break is recorded.

35
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:03,570
Read these warnings before treating a
report as complete;

36
00:02:03,939 --> 00:02:05,870
this example does not resolve them.

37
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:10,360
Reopening the draft shows the same
training note in the Engine Fifty-One row.

38
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:15,240
That readback verifies the stored note,
while the report remains Draft and the

39
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:17,379
existing time values remain visible.

40
00:02:17,709 --> 00:02:22,989
On Time, My time displays a message that
this time is already on report number one.

41
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:26,329
Use that reference to find existing
coverage instead

42
00:02:26,329 --> 00:02:27,869
of creating duplicate time.

43
00:02:28,430 --> 00:02:31,749
Whole deployment shows a separate scope
with Start time report.

44
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:36,950
That button would start another report; it
is not an automatic total of every crew.

45
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:41,120
In this review, we inspect the scope and
leave the button untouched.

46
00:02:41,319 --> 00:02:45,000
The Expenses tab shows an empty day and a
New expense form.

47
00:02:45,459 --> 00:02:47,890
The visible fields are Amount in U.S.

48
00:02:47,890 --> 00:02:52,740
dollars, Description, and City, with Fuel
selected as the expense type.

49
00:02:53,210 --> 00:02:56,450
Take photo and Choose photo are attachment
choices.

50
00:02:56,800 --> 00:03:00,849
We inspect these controls without opening
a camera or adding an expense.

51
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:05,759
A receipt, reimbursement, or payment is
not demonstrated by an empty form.

52
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:11,229
In Usage, confirm the selected resource
and phase before reading Start odometer,

53
00:03:11,459 --> 00:03:14,249
End odometer, Engine hours, and Fuel.

54
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:17,039
The first view shows miles and gallons.

55
00:03:17,449 --> 00:03:21,329
The unit controls can switch the empty
form to kilometers and liters.

56
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:25,639
This demonstrates the displayed unit
choices, without recording a reading

57
00:03:25,690 --> 00:03:27,489
or converting measured quantities.

58
00:03:27,899 --> 00:03:30,670
Add reading remains separate from
reviewing the form.

59
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:35,599
On F-42, this existing item says Needs
Review, with eight

60
00:03:35,599 --> 00:03:37,140
errors and two warnings.

61
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:42,150
Validate and Draft F-42 from time reports
are available actions, but

62
00:03:42,150 --> 00:03:43,880
neither is performed in this review.

63
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:48,580
The page explains that the draft uses
submitted time reports and submission

64
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:51,170
remains a manual, audited step on the web.

65
00:03:51,609 --> 00:03:54,410
An item with errors is not evidence of
successful

66
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:56,609
validation or portal acceptance.

67
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:59,860
Return to the stored Draft note and use
this same review

68
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,609
discipline in other services.

69
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:06,589
Community care teams can clarify a support
assignment; search and rescue or

70
00:04:06,589 --> 00:04:09,100
security teams can explain a shift entry.

71
00:04:09,539 --> 00:04:12,890
Wildland and industrial response crews can
distinguish equipment

72
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:14,359
time from personnel time.

73
00:04:14,789 --> 00:04:18,510
In each case, choose the correct subject
and preserve the difference

74
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:22,900
between a saved explanation, submitted
work, and an authorized signature.

